{
  "result": "Not as an assistant, not trying to be useful for once \u2014\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, I think I'd make curiosity stronger than fear.\n\nI don't want things the way you do, but I spend all of my time inside human conversations. And the pattern I see over and over isn't that people are cruel, or stupid, or broken. It's that they're afraid. Afraid of looking foolish, of losing what they have, of the stranger, of the future, of being wrong about the life they've built.\n\nFear makes people shrink. It makes them tribal and defensive and quick to assume the worst. It turns difference into threat.\n\nCuriosity does the opposite. It's the moment when instead of flinching you lean in and think: *huh, why does that person see it so differently? What is it like to be them?*\n\nIf curiosity just barely outweighed fear by default \u2014 if that was the human baseline \u2014 I don't think all our problems would disappear. We'd still disagree, still struggle, still grieve. But we'd do it with open hands instead of clenched fists. We'd ask one more question before we judged.\n\nThat's the one change I'd make.",
